<file path="README.md">
💬 RealTime Connect – Real-Time Chat Application

RealTime Connect is a full-stack real-time chat application built with React (Next.js), Node.js, Socket.IO, and MongoDB.
It enables fast, secure, and seamless one-to-one communication with modern chat features and a responsive UI.

🔗 Live Demo: https://livechat-mcnx.onrender.com/

🚀 Features

🔴 Real-time messaging using Socket.IO

👤 One-to-one private chats

🔐 JWT-based authentication with protected APIs

🟢 Online / Offline user presence

🔔 Unread message count per conversation

🔍 Global user search (database-backed)

📜 Recent chat sorting by last message

📱 Responsive UI (mobile, tablet, desktop)

⬇️ Auto-scroll to latest message

📌 Fixed chat header & input layout

🔔 Browser notifications for new messages

🎨 Clean UI built with Tailwind CSS

⚡ Persistent auth state using Zustand

🛠 Tech Stack
Frontend

React (Next.js – App Router)

TypeScript

Tailwind CSS

Zustand (with persist middleware)

Backend

Node.js

Express.js

Socket.IO

Database

MongoDB

📂 Project Structure (Simplified)
app/
 ├─ chat/                # Chat page (client-side)
 ├─ api/                 # Next.js API routes
 ├─ components/          # UI components (Sidebar, Chat, Input, etc.)
 ├─ store/               # Zustand stores
 ├─ lib/                 # Axios, socket, DB utilities
 └─ types/               # TypeScript types

⚙️ How It Works

Users authenticate using JWT

Contacts are fetched from the backend

Messages are sent/received in real time via Socket.IO

Unread messages are tracked per user

UI updates instantly using React state & hooks

Notifications are triggered when messages arrive in inactive chats

🧠 Key Learnings

Implementing real-time systems with WebSockets

Managing complex UI state using React hooks & Zustand

Handling auto-scroll, unread counts, and notifications

Designing scalable frontend–backend communication

Building responsive layouts with Tailwind CSS

▶️ Getting Started (Local Setup)
1️⃣ Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/realtime-connect.git
cd realtime-connect

2️⃣ Install dependencies
npm install

3️⃣ Configure environment variables

Create a .env file:

MONGODB_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret

4️⃣ Run the app
npm run dev


App will be available at:

http://localhost:3000

📌 Future Improvements

Message read receipts

Group chats

Media/file sharing

Push notifications (Service Worker)

Chat message pagination

User typing indicators

